window.docContents[193].resolve({"/ProofObjects/#Logical-Foundations--ProofObjects___-The-Curry-Howard-Correspondence--Logical-Connectives-as-Inductive-Types--Existential-Quantification":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo destruct existentials in a proof term we simply use match:\n\ntheorem dist_exists_or_term (α : Type) (P Q : α → Prop) :\n    (∃ x, P x ∨ Q x) → (∃ x, P x) ∨ (∃ x, Q x) :=\n  fun h => match h with\n           | Exists.intro x hx =>\n               match hx with\n               | Or.inl hpx => Or.inl (Exists.intro x hpx)\n               | Or.inr hqx => Or.inr (Exists.intro x hqx)\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009ProofObjects: The Curry-Howard Correspondence\u0009Logical Connectives as Inductive Types","header":"10.6.3. Existential Quantification","id":"/ProofObjects/#Logical-Foundations--ProofObjects___-The-Curry-Howard-Correspondence--Logical-Connectives-as-Inductive-Types--Existential-Quantification"}});